# Diagnostics from the skybox / background investigation, recovered from the
# working tree where they had been left unsaved.
#
# None of this changes what the game renders unless a switch is set; every
# addition is behind a getenv, and the default path through glxSend's packet
# loop is still a plain glx_DrawPacket(p).
#
#   OPENSTRIKERS_SKY_DEBUG=1            BasicStadium reports what the skybox and
#       clouds objects resolved to at init (hash, flags, bounding radius, model
#       pointer); world.cpp reports whether the Palace "hills" backdrop survives
#       the render loop and whether it is in the frustum.
#   OPENSTRIKERS_TRACE_LIGHTING=1       glxSend logs each distinct world/ambient
#       /material colour it packs, once per distinct value.
#   OPENSTRIKERS_TRACE_MISSING_TEXTURES=1  glxTexture reports every texture
#       handle that had to be resolved through an animation, once per pair.
#   OPENSTRIKERS_CHAR_RASTER_DEBUG=1    DrawableCharacter dumps the raster state
#       of the first few skin-mesh packets (depth test/write/func, alpha, blend,
#       cull, colour write).
#   OPENSTRIKERS_CHAR_DEPTHWRITE=1 / OPENSTRIKERS_CHAR_ZALWAYS=1   make the
#       character view write depth, or ignore it entirely. These were the A/B
#       for "distant geometry occludes near characters"; note that the
#       conclusion drawn from them at the time was later retracted.
#   OPENSTRIKERS_FIXED_STEP=<ms>        drives every task from a constant delta
#       instead of the wall clock, so two runs reach the same game state at the
#       same frame number. This is the closest thing to a deterministic capture
#       the port has -- but it does NOT make runs identical, so still do not
#       decide anything by diffing frame N of one run against frame N of
#       another.
